From: OpenWrt MT6990 repair <mt6990@local>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: size sparse EINT instances by index

The MT6990 SDK EINT table has sparse hardware indexes in instance 3.  Allocate
each instance lookup table through its highest hardware index instead of by
the number of populated pins, preventing an out-of-bounds write while keeping
the vendor pin-to-instance mapping intact.

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/mtk-eint.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/mtk-eint.c
@@ -520,7 +520,8 @@ int mtk_eint_do_init(struct mtk_eint *ei
 			if (inst >= eint->nbase)
 				continue;
-			eint->base_pin_num[inst]++;
+			eint->base_pin_num[inst] = max_t(u16,
+				eint->base_pin_num[inst], eint->pins[i].index + 1);
 		}
 	} else {
 
 	/*
